# XII. Translation-project output format

Every translated passage should produce six linked objects.

## 1. Source object

* Sanskrit
* segmentation
* morphology
* variant readings
* literal translation
* polished translation
* source location

## 2. Claim object

> What exactly is asserted?

No commentary yet.

## 3. Argument object

* premises;
* conclusion;
* suppressed premises;
* inference type;
* opponent addressed.

## 4. Explanandum object

> What phenomenon is this argument trying to explain?

Examples:

* memory content;
* remembered ownership;
* reflexivity;
* unity through change;
* other minds;
* meaningful determination.

## 5. Countermodel object

The strongest alternative explanation:

* Buddhist causal stream;
* Nyāya enduring plural selves;
* reflexivist minimal self;
* constructivist self-model;
* process ontology;
* predictive generative system.

## 6. Verdict object

* established;
* plausible;
* underdetermined;
* invalid;
* depends on disputed premise;
* outside formal proof.

This is the useful knowledge graph.

